WEBVTT

1
00:00:33.173 --> 00:00:37.473
[summoning whistle]

2
00:00:40.484 --> 00:00:44.396
<i>[whispered] Kristy...</i>

3
00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.640
Girl screams

4
00:01:30.045 --> 00:01:31.209
<i>[Echoing cry] Help me!</i>

5
00:01:41.609 --> 00:01:44.879
Screaming

6
00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:55.859
Whistling 'Jesus Loves Me'

7
00:01:55.995 --> 00:01:56.694
Screams

8
00:01:57.344 --> 00:02:00.121
Continues whistling...

9
00:02:13.594 --> 00:02:17.194
Whistling fades as music builds

10
00:02:23.781 --> 00:02:25.573
<i>[whispered] Kristy...!</i>

11
00:02:27.651 --> 00:02:31.602
<i>Police are still searching for 21 year old
college student Heather Price,</i>

12
00:02:31.722 --> 00:02:36.048
<i>reported missing three days ago after
leaving a friend's house in Mills Fall.</i>

13
00:02:36.168 --> 00:02:39.471
<i>At the time of her disappearance
Price was wearing a striped sweater,</i>

14
00:02:39.562 --> 00:02:41.343
<i>dark blue jeans and sneakers.</i>

15
00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.078
<i>Anyone who may have...</i>

16
00:02:45.908 --> 00:02:48.774
Terrified cries.

17
00:03:12.122 --> 00:03:13.568
<i>The time is now.</i>

18
00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.775
<i>Kill...Kristy.</i>

19
00:03:19.235 --> 00:03:22.100
<i>Kristy is a strong word of Christ.</i>

20
00:03:22.879 --> 00:03:26.376
<i>You kristy Kill,
you kill God.</i>

21
00:03:29.552 --> 00:03:31.263
<i>Kristy is pretty,</i>

22
00:03:32.055 --> 00:03:33.312
<i>pure...</i>

23
00:03:33.985 --> 00:03:35.199
<i>...blessed.</i>

24
00:03:41.509 --> 00:03:42.765
<i>Find them.</i>

25
00:03:48.453 --> 00:03:49.936
<i>Hunt them.</i>

26
00:03:53.538 --> 00:03:55.138
<i>Know their fear.</i>

27
00:04:17.396 --> 00:04:19.273
<i>Show your work.</i>

28
00:04:26.827 --> 00:04:28.711
<i>More will follow.</i>

29
00:04:35.136 --> 00:04:36.752
<i>They are weak.</i>

30
00:04:45.105 --> 00:04:49.661
<i>They...are
...Kristies.</i>

31
00:05:00.552 --> 00:05:03.153
"To see the world in a grain of sand"

32
00:05:03.339 --> 00:05:05.779
"And heaven in a wild flower"

33
00:05:06.226 --> 00:05:08.980
"Hold infinity in the palm of your hand"

34
00:05:09.358 --> 00:05:11.158
"And eternity in an hour"

35
00:05:11.983 --> 00:05:14.442
"A robin redbreast in a cage"

36
00:05:14.742 --> 00:05:15.742
"Puts..."

37
00:05:15.862 --> 00:05:19.406
- You're so immature!
- I'm laughing because you sound so bored.

38
00:05:19.459 --> 00:05:21.565
I'm not <i>bored</i>. I just...

39
00:05:22.199 --> 00:05:24.202
I don't get how to break it down.

40
00:05:24.319 --> 00:05:26.170
It's poetry you nerd...

41
00:05:26.269 --> 00:05:27.377
not math.

42
00:05:27.456 --> 00:05:29.117
Did you just call me a nerd?

43
00:05:29.192 --> 00:05:29.937
Yeah.

44
00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:34.533
It's not an equation. It's an experience.

45
00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:38.310
As far as poets go
Blake's pretty much a bad ass.

46
00:05:38.906 --> 00:05:40.507
You just need to...

47
00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.055
embrace it a little more.

48
00:05:44.082 --> 00:05:46.442
We're not all future novelists!

49
00:05:46.869 --> 00:05:48.459
Future novelist?

50
00:05:50.076 --> 00:05:51.125
I like that!

51
00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.196
Ok, well, I can't get
a B in this class.

52
00:05:54.242 --> 00:05:56.584
I have to keep my academic scholarship.

53
00:05:56.704 --> 00:06:00.576
- It'll be fine. I'll help you through it.
- No you have to get a head start. Remember?

54
00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:05.168
Come on!
You're the one who opted out.

55
00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.656
Aaron it's fine.
I got laid. You can go.

56
00:06:07.776 --> 00:06:09.553
Hell - bring Nicole if you want!

57
00:06:09.673 --> 00:06:11.553
It's silly that you guys are staying here.

58
00:06:12.076 --> 00:06:15.452
You think a long weekend
of girl time is silly?

59
00:06:15.627 --> 00:06:17.180
Actually it's kind of hot.

60
00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.305
It is and you're gonna miss it all.
Now get off the bed.

61
00:06:19.338 --> 00:06:21.245
I don't think so!

62
00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:38.610
Heisenberg was all about
unforeseen outcome.

63
00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:42.750
Light fending, sodium nitrate
exploding with water...

64
00:06:43.201 --> 00:06:44.007
Boom!

65
00:06:44.161 --> 00:06:46.718
That sounds like
an unexpected outcome to me. Yes?

66
00:06:53.867 --> 00:06:57.476
Oh, I know Mom. We talked about this.
The flights are so expensive.

67
00:06:57.572 --> 00:07:00.322
No they always jack it up
for the Thanksgiving.

68
00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:03.286
I said they jack it up.

69
00:07:03.492 --> 00:07:06.997
No I'll be fine until Christmas.
You have Tammy and the baby.

70
00:07:08.278 --> 00:07:09.872
Want these lights on Justine?

71
00:07:09.995 --> 00:07:10.928
Oh, uh...

72
00:07:11.074 --> 00:07:13.692
No you can turn them off.
I'm almost done.

73
00:07:14.182 --> 00:07:15.898
Just come. She won't bother us.
I swear.

74
00:07:15.978 --> 00:07:17.648
Aaron don't you remember the 4th of July

75
00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:20.675
when she asked me how
my dishwashing program was going?

76
00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:22.245
She doesn't get work-study.

77
00:07:22.285 --> 00:07:25.132
Oh. Does she understand that
some people have to work for a living?

78
00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.518
Jus!...
Stop.

79
00:07:26.713 --> 00:07:28.856
I swear to God
you can be so stubborn.

80
00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:31.670
You just tell me what you want!

81
00:07:33.197 --> 00:07:34.629
I want you to stay.

82
00:07:35.941 --> 00:07:37.040
With me.

83
00:07:38.026 --> 00:07:39.225
Just one time.

84
00:07:41.468 --> 00:07:42.990
You know my family.

85
00:07:43.728 --> 00:07:45.021
I have to go home.

86
00:07:45.141 --> 00:07:48.292
Einstein saw order in the universe

87
00:07:48.319 --> 00:07:50.778
and believe that
nothing happens by a chance.

88
00:07:50.838 --> 00:07:52.031
Whereas...

89
00:07:52.237 --> 00:07:55.644
Heisenberg believed that
the world was inherently chaotic,

90
00:07:55.889 --> 00:07:57.692
more random.

91
00:07:58.879 --> 00:08:00.636
I miss you guys too.

92
00:08:00.915 --> 00:08:02.089
Hey, Jus!

93
00:08:04.163 --> 00:08:07.576
Oh, it's just...
It's Scott the groundskeeper.

94
00:08:10.201 --> 00:08:11.901
Don't work too hard, huh?

95
00:08:14.204 --> 00:08:14.954
Okay.

96
00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:18.449
- Have a happy Thanksgiving.
- You too Greg.

97
00:08:18.975 --> 00:08:23.524
I think the Einstein quote was:
"God does not play dice with the universe."

98
00:08:23.711 --> 00:08:25.559
And in Heisenberg's world,...

99
00:08:25.843 --> 00:08:27.810
God does roll the dice.

100
00:08:29.362 --> 00:08:30.391
Say it.

101
00:08:30.552 --> 00:08:31.639
Say what?

102
00:08:32.924 --> 00:08:33.918
You know what.

103
00:08:41.072 --> 00:08:43.825
You can't corner me with technology.

104
00:08:44.684 --> 00:08:46.711
- Say it.
- Aaron come on!

105
00:08:47.054 --> 00:08:48.301
I love you.

106
00:08:50.125 --> 00:08:51.591
I love you Justine.

107
00:09:04.089 --> 00:09:05.239
Be safe.

108
00:09:20.076 --> 00:09:20.861
Go.

109
00:09:31.566 --> 00:09:32.424
Bye.

110
00:10:50.668 --> 00:10:53.403
- Hey Wayne! How are you doing?
- Hey! My stay behind!

111
00:10:53.463 --> 00:10:57.265
Doing my laundry
before I hit the books.
[Wayne chuckles]

112
00:11:31.745 --> 00:11:33.878
- Oh, oh!
- I am so sorry!

113
00:11:33.998 --> 00:11:35.746
- Are you okay?
- Oh yeah!

114
00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.070
No it's just this basement...

115
00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:40.350
So are...are these
gonna do this all weekend?

116
00:11:40.389 --> 00:11:41.876
Yeah that's what I heard.

117
00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.159
God...

118
00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.462
Oh, okay uh...

119
00:11:45.615 --> 00:11:46.210
Phew!

120
00:11:46.243 --> 00:11:48.655
So... you have room for one more?

121
00:11:49.269 --> 00:11:50.181
Thanks.

122
00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.482
- And don't forget the red wine?
- Uh, no. That's just the given.

123
00:11:53.532 --> 00:11:54.370
Bye.

124
00:11:57.211 --> 00:11:59.855
<i>...smashed and
there was blood on the tire.</i>

125
00:11:59.934 --> 00:12:04.241
<i>Investigators say personal items
were found in several dumpsters.</i>

126
00:12:04.412 --> 00:12:06.601
<i>While police are canvassing the area...</i>

127
00:12:06.677 --> 00:12:08.653
<i>...they won't comment whether
there is a connection...</i>

128
00:12:08.783 --> 00:12:12.321
<i>...to two young women who have been
recorded missing since late [Tuesday?].</i>

129
00:12:15.198 --> 00:12:16.548
Hi Anna!

130
00:12:16.754 --> 00:12:18.014
Are you going back to London?

131
00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.900
No just friends up state.

132
00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.461
You and Nicole really staying behind?

133
00:12:22.514 --> 00:12:25.313
[Sighs] Yeah - our turkey pot pie awaits...

134
00:12:25.577 --> 00:12:28.419
- Dasvidaniya!
- Happy Thanksgiving!

135
00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.519
Yeah it's all good.

136
00:12:30.927 --> 00:12:32.238
Dad! I know!

137
00:12:32.988 --> 00:12:34.687
Yeah...I'll be cool if she's cool.

138
00:12:35.409 --> 00:12:37.097
Ok. I'll see you soon.

139
00:12:37.745 --> 00:12:38.495
Love.

140
00:12:39.322 --> 00:12:40.154
No!

141
00:12:40.855 --> 00:12:42.861
Please don't kill me!
My dad is back.

142
00:12:42.914 --> 00:12:46.081
He surprised the family and he wants
to spend the holiday in Aspen.

143
00:12:46.565 --> 00:12:48.205
The car's on its way.

144
00:12:48.577 --> 00:12:49.644
Come with me!

145
00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.563
I get another plane ticket!

146
00:12:51.658 --> 00:12:53.683
You can't stay here all by yourself.

147
00:12:54.099 --> 00:12:54.932
Jus!

148
00:12:55.145 --> 00:12:57.155
It's okay.
I'm fine. Really.

149
00:12:58.121 --> 00:13:00.895
I am <i>so</i> sorry. I <i>swear</i>
I wanted to hang out with you.

150
00:13:00.922 --> 00:13:03.068
It's just my dad's taking a break
from the campaign,

151
00:13:03.101 --> 00:13:05.585
and the whole family's gonna be together,
and it's like <i>Aspen</i>!

152
00:13:05.629 --> 00:13:07.529
Nicole: I understand!
It's fine!

153
00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.111
Family's family.

154
00:13:09.799 --> 00:13:12.062
And promise me
you will get off this campus.

155
00:13:12.102 --> 00:13:14.529
Get some fresh air somewhere <i>away</i>!

156
00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.509
Here.

157
00:13:16.515 --> 00:13:17.379
Take my baby.

158
00:13:17.451 --> 00:13:19.152
I don't even want to breath
on your Beamer [BMW].

159
00:13:19.192 --> 00:13:20.554
Oh please! Use it!

160
00:13:20.645 --> 00:13:22.346
You know you want to.

161
00:13:23.166 --> 00:13:24.015
Thanks.

162
00:13:24.794 --> 00:13:26.475
Oh! Come here.

163
00:13:27.875 --> 00:13:29.802
- You be safe. Okay?
- Ok.

164
00:13:30.942 --> 00:13:32.395
- Thank you.
- Uh huh.

165
00:13:32.562 --> 00:13:33.443
- OK.
- Bye.

166
00:13:33.518 --> 00:13:35.065
[Laughs] Hey - last chance!

167
00:13:35.331 --> 00:13:36.365
Oh!

168
00:13:38.202 --> 00:13:39.106
Thanks.

169
00:13:40.338 --> 00:13:41.278
Bye.

170
00:13:44.652 --> 00:13:46.397
See you after Thanksgiving!

171
00:13:46.488 --> 00:13:48.162
Thanks for the Beamer!

172
00:14:01.408 --> 00:14:05.484
<i>[Radio host] Good morning and Happy Thanksgiving
from everyone here at 106.5!</i>

173
00:14:05.538 --> 00:14:08.344
<i>[2nd voice] That's right. And hopefully everyone is spending
it with their family and friends.</i>

174
00:14:08.384 --> 00:14:09.384
<i>What do you think Jimbo?</i>

175
00:14:09.424 --> 00:14:12.429
<i>[1st Host] Oh man. It is a <b>beautiful</b> morning
- perfect for Thanksgiving.

176
00:14:12.533 --> 00:14:15.919
<i>[2nd Host] Hm-hmmm. But then you are actually on for
some rain later this evening,</i>

177
00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:18.267
<i>just about the time everyone should be [chatter fades]</i>

178
00:14:21.393 --> 00:14:23.692
<i>-[1st Host] Let it rain!
   -[2nd Host] Let it rain! let it rain!</i>

179
00:15:56.485 --> 00:15:57.274
Hey.

180
00:15:57.504 --> 00:15:58.933
No I'm having fun.

181
00:15:59.053 --> 00:16:01.677
Nicole just went out to Market Max
to get some more snacks.

182
00:16:02.691 --> 00:16:03.990
How's dinner?

183
00:16:04.503 --> 00:16:06.777
Uh...turkey pot pie

184
00:16:06.934 --> 00:16:09.630
...red vines - proper holiday feast.

185
00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:12.961
We're saving the wine for later.

186
00:16:14.548 --> 00:16:15.684
I don't know. I'm...

187
00:16:15.879 --> 00:16:18.078
...having a hard time
with that one.

188
00:16:20.815 --> 00:16:23.414
Oh really quiet here.
It's really peaceful.

189
00:17:23.144 --> 00:17:24.388
What the hell!

190
00:17:30.864 --> 00:17:32.503
Hey Wayne - those lights are out again.

191
00:17:32.636 --> 00:17:35.307
Yeah. I phoned a systems check.
They're running a wire...

192
00:17:35.374 --> 00:17:37.507
...but the crews won't be back until Monday.

193
00:17:38.923 --> 00:17:39.990
Ah!

194
00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:42.029
Taking Nicolle's little pony
out for a spin?

195
00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:43.013
Yep.

196
00:17:43.467 --> 00:17:45.971
Max or Ben & Jerry's calling my name.

197
00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:47.092
Oh. Copy that.

198
00:17:47.211 --> 00:17:49.862
- Can I get you anything?
- No I'm cool.

199
00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:53.119
Are you sure?
You're my Thanksgiving bud.

200
00:17:54.702 --> 00:17:55.653
Mountain Dew?

201
00:17:56.147 --> 00:17:57.491
Pumpkin pie?

202
00:17:57.632 --> 00:17:59.832
Soda and pumpkin pie.
Done!

203
00:18:00.546 --> 00:18:04.147
Hey, uh, make sure David at the gates knows
that you're on a stay behind.

204
00:18:04.694 --> 00:18:06.971
OK. Thanks Wayne.
Bye.

205
00:18:43.876 --> 00:18:46.596
Hi. I'm Justine Wills. I'm the stay behind?

206
00:18:46.702 --> 00:18:48.242
Right. You got your swipe?

207
00:18:48.391 --> 00:18:49.090
Yeah.

208
00:18:49.269 --> 00:18:51.170
Good because I'm gonna close
the gate in an hour.

209
00:18:51.289 --> 00:18:53.492
Oh it's okay - I'll be back in 20.

210
00:18:53.613 --> 00:18:54.645
Thanks.

211
00:19:09.144 --> 00:19:11.208
<i>More on the Heather Price store as it develops...</i>

212
00:19:11.327 --> 00:19:13.640
<i>...but on the lighter note,
early shoppers standing in line...</i>

213
00:19:13.686 --> 00:19:17.420
<i>...for those Black Friday sales will need
plenty of tents and strong umbrellas</i>

214
00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:21.086
<i>'cause we've got some nasty weather
moving in tonight care of a low pressure...</i>

215
00:21:40.959 --> 00:21:41.808
Thank you.

216
00:21:44.601 --> 00:21:46.151
[Violet] I like your car.

217
00:21:51.859 --> 00:21:53.248
You're so pretty.

218
00:21:59.518 --> 00:22:00.762
Student right?

219
00:22:00.883 --> 00:22:01.667
Yeah.

220
00:22:12.291 --> 00:22:15.659
Yo Rockstar - if you're not gonna
buy anything you need to boogie.

221
00:22:19.291 --> 00:22:21.342
How much are these sunglasses?

222
00:22:21.758 --> 00:22:23.609
What does price tag say?

223
00:22:27.525 --> 00:22:29.115
I want a discount.

224
00:22:29.391 --> 00:22:31.240
Let's see your ID.

225
00:22:36.368 --> 00:22:38.200
[demands] I want a discount.

226
00:22:39.509 --> 00:22:41.119
Hey, look, I'll pay.

227
00:22:42.082 --> 00:22:43.131
I'll pay.

228
00:22:46.356 --> 00:22:48.114
I don't want anything from you.

229
00:22:51.017 --> 00:22:54.967
All right. You try to do something nice
to someone and this the shit you get.

230
00:22:58.210 --> 00:23:00.299
You don't know what shit is...

231
00:23:01.988 --> 00:23:03.750
[whispers] Kristy.

232
00:23:04.268 --> 00:23:05.667
<i>You're</i> the one!

233
00:24:23.747 --> 00:24:24.933
Jesus!

234
00:25:45.290 --> 00:25:46.384
Hey!

235
00:25:49.066 --> 00:25:50.115
You all good?

236
00:25:50.314 --> 00:25:51.973
There are some people out there.

237
00:25:52.054 --> 00:25:54.886
A bunch of bored townies doing
Thanksgiving huh?

238
00:25:55.733 --> 00:25:58.038
- I don't know.
- Did they follow you? Are you okay?

239
00:25:58.157 --> 00:26:00.410
No I don't think they followed me.
It's just...

240
00:26:00.683 --> 00:26:03.037
It was weird. I think they were just trying to scare me.

241
00:26:03.644 --> 00:26:04.497
All right.

242
00:26:04.798 --> 00:26:07.098
We got your back in here all right?
You know that?

243
00:26:07.261 --> 00:26:08.828
Yeah. I know you do.

244
00:26:09.160 --> 00:26:10.172
I got <i>your</i> back.

245
00:26:10.291 --> 00:26:11.588
Good 'looking out'...

246
00:26:12.015 --> 00:26:14.565
- Good night Wayne.
- Good night dear.

247
00:26:47.855 --> 00:26:48.705
<i>Hello?</i>

248
00:26:48.892 --> 00:26:50.041
Hey! What's up?

249
00:26:50.355 --> 00:26:51.804
<i>Hey! You all right?</i>

250
00:26:52.287 --> 00:26:52.987
Yeah.

251
00:26:53.984 --> 00:26:55.184
Why? I just...

252
00:26:55.929 --> 00:26:58.479
I don't know.
I just want to hear your voice.

253
00:26:59.273 --> 00:27:01.173
I had this weird thing happen.

254
00:27:01.355 --> 00:27:02.654
<i>What happened?</i>

255
00:27:10.529 --> 00:27:11.769
<i>You're...by yourself?</i>

256
00:27:11.988 --> 00:27:12.863
